# Native left-sleeve study — REJECTED, private only

Root reviewed V2 and rejected the inflated, smooth sleeve. Keep the evidence; do not publish this body or its source patch.

The sleeve uses the current Granadero coat topology. Its collar, shoulder yoke, strap support, cuff, native body, rig and animation library remain fixed. The unchanged current generated skin and hat are included in every before/after frame.

The pilot replaces the left sleeve's fixed elbow ridges with a broader cloth envelope. It adds two shallow oblique folds on the inner elbow through one angle-driven corrective. The outer elbow stays smooth. The maximum rest-envelope displacement is 15 mm. The two fold displacements at the authored bend are −1.88 to +3.61 mm.

## Visible result

The hard elbow notch is removed. The extra cloth volume is useful, particularly in pistol aim and rifle loading. It is still quite round. The two inner folds are subtle at the 700-pixel whole-body view. This is a local construction improvement, not proof that the whole uniform now reads as realistic woven cloth.

